===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|annuli}}

# A [[ring#Noun|ring]]- or [[donut]]-[[shaped#Adjective|shaped]] [[area]] or [[structure#Noun|structure]].
#: {{hyponyms|en|torus}}
#* {{RQ:Sterne Tristram Shandy|volume=III|chapter=IX|pages=29–30|pageref=30|passage=But by the knots I am ſpeaking of, may it pleaſe your reverences to believe, that I mean good, honeſt, deviliſh tight, hard knots, made ''bona fide'', as ''{{w|Obadiah}}'' made his;—in vvhich there is no quibbling proviſion made by the duplication and return of the tvvo ends of the ſtrings through the '''annulus''' or nooſe made by the ſecond ''implication'' of them— {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|anatomy}}{{lb|en|anatomy}} A ring of [[fibrous]] [[tissue#Noun|tissue]]; specifically {{lb|en|cardiology}}, such a ring around an [[opening#Noun|opening]] of a [[heart#Noun|heart]] [[valve#Noun|valve]], to which the valve [[leaflet#Noun|leaflets]] and [[muscle fiber|muscle fibres]] of the [[atrium|atria]] and [[ventricle]]s are [[attach]]ed; an [[annulus fibrosus cordis]].
# {{senseid|en|astronomy}}{{lb|en|astronomy}} A ring of [[light#Noun|light]] in a [[celestial body]], especially when [[cause#Verb|caused]] by an [[annular eclipse]] (for example, when the [[Sun]] and [[Moon]] are [[in line]] with the [[Earth]], but the Moon does not [[completely]] [[cover#Verb|cover]] the Sun's [[disc#Noun|disc]]).
# {{lb|en|biology}}
## {{senseid|en|botany}}{{lb|en|botany}} A structure [[surround#Verb|surrounding]] a [[sporangium]] (or [[part#Noun|part]] of it) which [[shrink#Verb|shrinks]] and causes it to [[rupture#Verb|rupture]] for [[spore#Noun|spore]] [[dispersal]]; specifically, in a [[fern]]: a structure around about [[two-thirds]] of the sporangium [[consist#Verb|consisting]] of [[differentially]] [[thick#Adjective|thick]]-[[walled#Adjective|walled]] [[cell#Noun|cells]] which [[dry#Verb|dry]] and [[distort#Verb|distort]] the sporangium; and in a [[moss#Noun|moss]]: a [[complete#Adjective|complete]] ring of cells around the [[tip#Noun|tip]] of the sporangium which [[dissolve#Verb|dissolves]] to cause the tip to [[detach]].
## {{senseid|en|mycology}}{{lb|en|mycology}} The [[membranous]] [[remnant#Noun|remnants]] of a [[partial veil]] which [[leave#Verb|leaves]] a ring on the [[stem#Noun|stem]] of a [[mushroom#Noun|mushroom]].
# {{lb|en|mathematics}}
## {{senseid|en|geometry}}{{lb|en|geometry}} The [[region]] in a [[plane#Noun|plane]] between [[two#Numeral|two]] [[concentric]] [[circle#Noun|circles]] of [[different#Adjective|different]] [[radius|radii]].
## {{lb|en|topology}} Any [[topological space]] [[homeomorphic]] to the region in a plane between two concentric circles of different radii.
##: {{synonyms|en|cylinder}}
# {{senseid|en|technology}}{{lb|en|technology}} In a [[well#Noun|well]] such as an [[oil well]] or [[water#Noun|water]] well: the [[space#Noun|space]] between a [[pipe#Noun|pipe]] or [[tube#Noun|tube]] and any pipe, tube, [[casing#Noun|casing]], or [[side#Noun|sides]] of a [[hole#Noun|hole]] [[surround#Verb|surrounding]] it.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=September|title=Notes and News: Pneumatic Buffer Stop, E.R.|journal=Railway Magazine|page=642|text=Pressure balance is obtained by the air pressure in the cylinder operating on a supplementary piston in the buffer piston head, transmitting pressure to a small quantity of oil which is ported to an '''annulus''' between the buffer piston seals and the cylinder wall, so that the seal is always under opposing pressures; oil on one side and air on the other.}}                                                                 

